{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/263521-phosphorus-the-new-refinement-in-2e","id":263521,"title":"Phosphorus: The New Refinement in 2e","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Promethean: The Created"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-09-23T01:01:28-07:00","id":263521,"title":"Phosphorus: The New Refinement in 2e","content":"We don't know too much about Promethean 2e yet. What we <i>do</i> know is that there will be 10 Refinements, and one of them will be the brand spankin' new Refinement of Phosphorus. But what does that <i>mean??</i><br /> <br /> I did a bit of digging (read: cursory Wikipedia diving) and found some very interesting tidbits!<br /> <br /> Phosphorus was the first element to be &quot;discovered&quot; that ancient alchemists (the Greeks and Egyptians, most likely) hadn't known about. It comes in many colors and forms, but none of them occur &quot;in nature&quot; because phosphorus is <b>highly</b> reactive. In fact, white phosphorus catches fire just by <i>being exposed to oxygen</i>, and it burns bright and hot. Even when safely in a vacuum, phosphorus glows thanks to a phenomenon we now know as chemiluminescence.<br /> <br /> Which brings me to the name. Phosphorus was originally the name the ancient Greeks gave to the morning star, and it roughly translates to &quot;light-bringer&quot;. Any idea what the name of Phosphorus' Roman equivalent is?<br /> <br /> Damn right: it's Lucifer.<br /> <br /> And apparently phosphorus was known as &quot;the devil's element&quot; in it's day. It's a necessary ingredient in explosives and some nasty toxins (including nerve agents) -- and yet it's also necessary for life. It's one of the major things that comprises modern fertilizers, our bones and teeth are full of the stuff, and it's an essential part of <i>every living cell</i> due to its role in energy transference.<br /> <br /> So what does <i>this</i> mean? Perhaps there's something to be said about the paradoxical nature of phosphorus. It's everywhere, but also nowhere. It's required for life, yet also takes it. It's deeply ingrained in the system, but named after one of the most famous rebels.<br /> <br /> Any other ideas on what the Refinement of Phosphorus may bring us?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Cxuog44JenzbN7GaAyRqDO4DXce9VGv6ybaCv9yYsPk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Simulacre: An Alternative Morality Stat for Prometheans</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/9523-the-alchemy-lab-homebrew-athanors\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew Athanors</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/887-metamurpho","name":"Metamurpho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar887_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-23T02:45:39-07:00","id":263556,"title":"","content":"If it's &quot;devil-element&quot;, maybe it' about Vices of humans? If in <i>Aurum</i> the Created is trying to be the best of humans, to dedicated rather to Virtue of people, maybe <i>Phosphorus</i> is more about little failures of humanity. It's very human to be jealous, to be envy, to lust for someone. Not maybe proud of, but it <b>is</b> human element.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 09-23-2014, 07:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-23T04:08:57-07:00","id":263578,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/263521-phosphorus-the-new-refinement-in-2e?p=263556#post263556\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If it's &quot;devil-element&quot;, maybe it' about Vices of humans? If in <i>Aurum</i> the Created is trying to be the best of humans, to dedicated rather to Virtue of people, maybe <i>Phosphorus</i> is more about little failures of humanity. It's very human to b jelous, to be envy, to lust for someone. Not maybe proud of, but it <b>is</b> human element.</div> </div> </div> </div>Like the Cobalus refinement, you mean?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-23T04:13:08-07:00","id":263580,"title":"","content":"Read only <b>Promethean</b> corebook, didn't know it was Refinement for that before. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-23T06:51:17-07:00","id":263730,"title":"","content":"Yeah, Cobalus and the Contamination Transmutations is pretty much what you're describing, wyrd. It does some interesting stuff like sniffing out someone's Vice and getting psychic flashes of the worst thing someone's done, as well as making people act out on base desires. I wouldn't rule out anything just yet though, because...<br /> <br /> I have only just now done my basic math: with the 6 Refinements presented in the corebook and the 4 in Magnum Opus, the addition of Phosphorus to the roster means that at least one of the published Refinements as we know them is gonna go bye-bye. Naturally I think there's going to be some shuffling about of themes and concepts, and we certainly have no idea what Transmutations will be like, so I don't think anything's off the table just yet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Cxuog44JenzbN7GaAyRqDO4DXce9VGv6ybaCv9yYsPk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Simulacre: An Alternative Morality Stat for Prometheans</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/9523-the-alchemy-lab-homebrew-athanors\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew Athanors</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/887-metamurpho","name":"Metamurpho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar887_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-23T06:53:29-07:00","id":263732,"title":"","content":"If Cobalus is about understanding the moral frailties of humanity, then perhaps Phosphorus is about acting on them? A sort of intersection between Aurum, Cobalus, and Centimani? A Refinement for evil deeds, but of human evil, rather than the monstrosity of the Hundred-Handed","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/665-shkspr1048","name":"shkspr1048","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"630"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-23T07:39:50-07:00","id":263766,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Metamurpho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/263521-phosphorus-the-new-refinement-in-2e?p=263730#post263730\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have only just now done my basic math: with the 6 Refinements presented in the corebook and the 4 in Magnum Opus, the addition of Phosphorus to the roster means that at least one of the published Refinements as we know them is gonna go bye-bye. Naturally I think there's going to be some shuffling about of themes and concepts, and we certainly have no idea what Transmutations will be like, so I don't think anything's off the table just yet.</div> </div> </div> </div>i wouldn't think so, i would just think that they would make centimani just antagonists, also wouldn't this new Refinement have Alchemincus?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":3742,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","user":"Iceblade44","date":". 09-23-2014, 12:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-23T08:49:27-07:00","id":263813,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Metamurpho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/263521-phosphorus-the-new-refinement-in-2e?p=263730#post263730\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have only just now done my basic math: with the 6 Refinements presented in the corebook and the 4 in Magnum Opus, the addition of Phosphorus to the roster means that at least one of the published Refinements as we know them is gonna go bye-bye.</div> </div> </div> </div>Having just reread Magnum Opus about a month ago, I have to say I'm not sad to see Aes go.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 09-23-2014, 11:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-23T14:02:15-07:00","id":264102,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>shkspr1048</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/263521-phosphorus-the-new-refinement-in-2e?p=263732#post263732\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If Cobalus is about understanding the moral frailties of humanity, then perhaps Phosphorus is about acting on them? A sort of intersection between Aurum, Cobalus, and Centimani? A Refinement for evil deeds, but of human evil, rather than the monstrosity of the Hundred-Handed</div> </div> </div> </div>...Sort of like the yang to the yin, yeah; I can definitely see that. All humans must contend with their id, so why not explore that with a Refinement named after the Original Bad Boy? Why not strike up a rebellion as easily as you'd strike up a match? (Phosphorus is also used a lot in matches)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/263521-phosphorus-the-new-refinement-in-2e?p=263813#post263813\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Having just reread Magnum Opus about a month ago, I have to say I'm not sad to see Aes go.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wanted to like Beneficence really badly, but yeah -- it doesn't have the oomph. Promethean-as-support character is a really interesting space I'd still like to see explored, though.<br /> <br /> You also made me think of another thing, Satch: IIRC, we don't know of any other Refinements that will be in the game yet! So far the only confirmed one is Phosphorus. I couldn't find that original post to confirm, but that's certainly something to chew on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Cxuog44JenzbN7GaAyRqDO4DXce9VGv6ybaCv9yYsPk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Simulacre: An Alternative Morality Stat for Prometheans</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/9523-the-alchemy-lab-homebrew-athanors\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew Athanors</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/887-metamurpho","name":"Metamurpho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar887_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-23T18:11:29-07:00","id":264300,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Metamurpho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/263521-phosphorus-the-new-refinement-in-2e?p=264102#post264102\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wanted to like Beneficence really badly, but yeah -- it doesn't have the oomph. Promethean-as-support character is a really interesting space I'd still like to see explored, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>My reread more soured me on the Refinement on the grounds that when your sample character is being <i>flagrantly taken advantage of</i>, an anecdotal character <i>kills their throngmate after they cross the finish line</i>, and the Stereotypes viewpoint character is <i>the most obnoxious passive-aggressive fucker in recent memory</i>, you don't exactly want to join the Refinement that hardly any Promethean starts out on.<br /> <br /> I'll forgo that sort of medic for my can't-pick-your-friends rare-gathering-of-misfits band of pilgrims if it's all the same, thanks.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You also made me think of another thing, Satch: IIRC, we don't know of any other Refinements that will be in the game yet! So far the only confirmed one is Phosphorus. I couldn't find that original post to confirm, but that's certainly something to chew on. </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/230252-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-firestorm-chronicles?p=237081#post237081\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...081#post237081</a><br /> <br /> Been a while, but it's been there. Aes being dropped is purely speculation on my part, but it seems the most likely candidate if ten means ten and not eleven.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-23T20:09:10-07:00","id":264357,"title":"","content":"It\u2019s also possible that Phosphorus might be a reworking of Centimani into something that\u2019s not quite so \u201cthe Antagonist Refinement\u201d.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-23T20:51:14-07:00","id":264370,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/263521-phosphorus-the-new-refinement-in-2e?p=264357#post264357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It\u2019s also possible that Phosphorus might be a reworking of Centimani into something that\u2019s not quite so \u201cthe Antagonist Refinement\u201d.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think many of us place odds on that, the Centimani being lightened up from Antagonist.<br /> <br /> Okay, actually, let's change that to I wouldn't place odds on that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-23T21:40:22-07:00","id":264381,"title":"","content":"Isn't Phosphorus going to have something to do with light and manipulating it? I thought I read that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/740-anaximander","name":"Anaximander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar740_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"241"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-24T00:32:48-07:00","id":264433,"title":"","content":"What Matt said at GenCon was that Promethean 2e would be featuring all the Refinements, plus Phosphorus - that is, none of them are getting dropped.<br /> <br /> Phosphorus itself is apparently about light, shadows, and possibly death.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-24T04:18:57-07:00","id":264494,"title":"","content":"Over the years, a <i>lot</i> of people have expressed a wish for a Pilgrimmage towards superhumanity rather than humanity - something I think should get a most as much shrift as Golconda in Vampire.<br /> <br /> But a Refinement that's highly reactive, unknown to conventional alchemy (which is an accurate description of Prometheans), and associated with the world's most famous rebel against diviven purpose (and Mortality does seem to be what Prometheans are &quot;meant,&quot; whatever it is that's doing the meaning, to seek). Maybe something other than human is what it's after.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure how that ties into &quot;light, shadows, and possibly death,&quot; though. But one thing that occurs to me is the physical world. We have the study of humanity (Gold), self (Copper), Pyros (Mercury), the Promethean form (Lead), and other supernaturals (Silver) - but nothing covering the world - matter, forces, phsyics.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-27T13:57:00-07:00","id":266973,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/263521-phosphorus-the-new-refinement-in-2e?p=264494#post264494\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Over the years, a <i>lot</i> of people have expressed a wish for a Pilgrimmage towards superhumanity rather than humanity</div> </div> </div> </div>I think they may have missed the point of Promethean just a <i>wee</i> bit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-27T18:10:48-07:00","id":267096,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/263521-phosphorus-the-new-refinement-in-2e?p=266973#post266973\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think they may have missed the point of Promethean just a <i>wee</i> bit.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm one of those people and I don't feel I missed a point of <b>Promethan</b>. Just like using <b>Mage</b> for something other than &quot;my PC will lament on hard choices&quot; or <b>Werewolf</b> on playing destruction, killing machine. In setting, story wise, there are needed characters that have different goals than majority of PCs. In <b>Mage</b> there are Hubris driven mages, that makes those Bad Decisions that sunken the Atlantis and created Abyss. In <b>Werewolf </b>are those imbalanced Uratha that couldn't reconcile they Human and Wolf side. In <b>Vampire</b> those are guys that lost a touch with they humanity. And all this choices, even if somehow pointed as not desired for \u201cnormal populaces\u201d, should be interesting and viable options from PCs perspective. Because otherwise they don\u2019t tempt them to go with it.<br /> <br /> For me uninteresting is \u201cI won\u2019t become human, so I become serial killer\u201c ( Centimani ). Much more interesting is \u201cI won\u2019t become human, so I become something more\u201d. And this transhumanist approach think <i>Phosphorus</i> is, with Cobalus being about downsides of humans lives.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-27T18:30:01-07:00","id":267103,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/263521-phosphorus-the-new-refinement-in-2e?p=267096#post267096\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For me uninteresting is \u201cI won\u2019t become human, so I become serial killer\u201c ( Centimani ).</div> </div> </div> </div>The fact that your parenthetical doesn't describe the Hundred-Handed only serves to underline the matter of your disinterest being self-inflicted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-27T18:59:09-07:00","id":267125,"title":"","content":"Indeed; in the summary of the various Refinements, the core book describes the Centimani as seeking to master Flux, so as to tame the Pandoran Transmutations. In their write-up, the emphasis is on how they have a tendency to become more and more inhuman both physically and mentally \u2014 it\u2019s always a danger that when you seek to \u201ctranscend humanity\u201d, you\u2019re going to lose touch with humanity; and if you\u2019ve never had a firm grasp on what humanity is to begin with, it can\u2019t end well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-27T19:29:56-07:00","id":267137,"title":"","content":"Literally went to my bookshelf and reread a Centimani description. I see part of transhuman philosophy in it, but it's always connected to idea &quot;going for something different than human is madness&quot;. And this miss the point of &quot;transhuman as PCs&quot; - clearly Cetimani are antagonistic, not &quot;misguided&quot; for other Pilgrimage. There was good example on transhuman Promethean character concept - a Robocop. He want's to be more than human to best serve his community. He don't want to return to his old life - he knows he can't - but will make as much of it's existence as he can. Go to 10, not 11.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Promethean the Created</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Those Prometheans driven to understand Flux are degraded creatures \u2014 or at least, that is what Prometheans tell one another, when their paths cross. To seek to understand Flux, the power of division and chaos, which stands at the opposite pole from the unifying principle of Azoth, is a gateway to madness, surely. If Mortality can be achieved by striving toward and understanding the Azoth, how can the quest to comprehend the Flux end in anything but the creation of a true monster?<br /> <br /> <b>Overview</b><br /> Those who seek to understand Flux are creatures of incredible passion. That passion may be an all-consuming loneliness, driving them to seek communion with the <br /> very horrors that would tear them apart to feed on the Azoth within them. It may be a grief born of one failure <br /> after another to understand the nuances of humanity. After being faced, time and again, with the proof of one\u2019s monstrosity, it takes a very strong soul to not embrace <br /> that monstrosity. Others, perhaps the true philosophers of the Promethean sort, say that to understand the light, one must delve into the darkness, seeking to understand Azoth by discovering the nuances of Flux.<br /> Regardless of why they practice it, those who walk the path of the Centimani, the Hundred-Handed, consider themselves <br /> heirs to the legacy of the ancient monsters of old. Inhuman and monstrously strong, they delve into the horrors they are capable of <br /> with a thirst that sickens those who value the precepts of human morality.</div> </div> </div> </div>To say in <b>Promethean</b> tongue, our possible transhuman Refienment would want to maximized Azoth, not dedicate to Flux only.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-27T20:15:10-07:00","id":267146,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/263521-phosphorus-the-new-refinement-in-2e?p=267137#post267137\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Literally went to my bookshelf and reread a Centimani description. I see part of transhuman philosophy in it, but it's always connected to idea &quot;going for something different than human is madness&quot;. And this miss the point of &quot;transhuman as PCs&quot; - clearly Cetimani are antagonistic, not &quot;misguided&quot; for other Pilgrimage.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah yes, the &quot;clearly antagonistic&quot; characters of &quot;guy with an eye on his hand who just watches horrible shit happen,&quot; &quot;guy who's gone through all of the other five main Refinements and is implied to only have not reached his New Dawn due to the same detached-observer attitude that means he's a perfectly reasonable individual who happens to be a practitioner of Flux,&quot; and &quot;guy who's pretty much just given up on his own Pilgrimage because he's happier experimenting with variations on the generative act.&quot; These are certainly greater threats than any of the folks who adhere to an entire philosophy that can be described as &quot;be a revenge-fueled vindictive necrobot&quot; or &quot;poke the all-pervading madness-fire.&quot;<br /> <br /> I've said it about Werewolf and I'll say it about Promethean: going by the 1e corebook alone is a shitty metric to use for what 2e is likely to take cues from.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 09-27-2014, 11:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-27T22:00:45-07:00","id":267196,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/263521-phosphorus-the-new-refinement-in-2e?p=267137#post267137\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Literally went to my bookshelf and reread a Centimani description. I see part of transhuman philosophy in it, but it's always connected to idea &quot;going for something different than human is madness&quot;. And this miss the point of &quot;transhuman as PCs&quot; - clearly Cetimani are antagonistic, not &quot;misguided&quot; for other Pilgrimage. There was good example on transhuman Promethean character concept - a Robocop. He want's to be more than human to best serve his community. He don't want to return to his old life - <span style=\"color:red\">he knows he can't</span> - but will make as much of it's existence as he can. Go to 10, not 11.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mentioned this the last time Robocop was mentioned: the crucial difference between Robocop and a Promethean is that Robocop <i>can\u2019t</i> become human; a Promethean <i>can</i>. If an enterprising scientist in the Robocop setting were to announce that he could now clone biological replacements for all of Robocop\u2019s mechanical parts and restore him to being Alex Murphy, Robocop would likely take him up on the offer, sacrificing all of the bionic upgrades he received for a chance to be human again. <br /> <br /> The other difference is that Robocop already knows what it\u2019s like to be human, as he\u2019s already been one; a Promethean has, at best, a few fleeting residual memories from the body\u2019s prior host. <br /> <br /> All that, <i>and</i> <b>Robocop</b> goes with the notion that Robocop is Alex Murphy clawing his way back from the dead; in that regard, it has more in common with <b>Mummy</b> than with <b>Promethean</b>. <br /> <br /> The Centimani is already the transhumanist Refinement; Azoth is geared toward achieving the New Dawn and becoming human, and is covered by Mercurius. The reason why the Centimani come across in such a negative light is that even if you buy into the notion that \u201ctranshuman\u201d is better than \u201chuman\u201d (<i>not</i> an assumption <b>Promethean</b> makes), trying to skip straight from \u201cproto-human\u201d to \u201ctranshuman\u201d is about as smart as trying to run before you\u2019ve learned how to walk. The Centimani tend to be monsters because they don\u2019t put a high priority on the one thing that would prevent them from being monsters; they try to build a tower without first laying the foundation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-28T04:15:31-07:00","id":267304,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Neall:</b> I think they may have missed the point of Promethean just a wee bit. </div> </div> </div>I don't disagree. As I said, at most as much shrift as Golconda for Vampire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-28T13:22:37-07:00","id":267647,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/263521-phosphorus-the-new-refinement-in-2e?p=264494#post264494\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Over the years, a <i>lot</i> of people have expressed a wish for a Pilgrimmage towards superhumanity rather than humanity-</div> </div> </div> </div>That's really not what Promethean's about.<br /> <br /> Those people should go play Mage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-28T13:54:57-07:00","id":267667,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Pilgrimages that end with something other than humanity&quot; should be a thing, but that's less a &quot;core rule book&quot; thing and more a &quot;Supplement dedicated exclusively to that topic, with multiple methods and multiple end results, with an even mix of better/worse/or equal to human end results&quot; thing.<br /> <br /> Does that make sense?</div> </div> </div> </div>Thing is, we have rumors sections for that - Strange Alchemies' Refinements chapter has three rumors for each of the five main Refinements, and at least three of those fifteen rumors concern a Promethean becoming something other than human.<br /> <br /> Look at how many people think the inevitable Mage endgame is to archmastery followed by Ascension. Wordcount allocation shapes reader perception.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-28T14:01:33-07:00","id":267669,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/263521-phosphorus-the-new-refinement-in-2e?p=267647#post267647\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">That's really not what Promethean's about.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">Those people should go play Mage.</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\"><b>Mage</b> is great for high transhuman elements, like Singulairty, Strong A.I. or reality bending. But for more &quot;grounded&quot; stuff, like superstrenght, indestructibility or nano treatment the <b>Promethean</b> is far better. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">Not to mention what I said before - those of Created that forsake humanity for perfection in they unhuman state make a nice contrast for characters that </span></span><b><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">want </span></span></b><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">to become mortal. It rise questions &quot;why do you really do it&quot;? &quot;Is it more than angels making you&quot;? &quot;Why would any one don't agree with your point&quot;? For me it's much more drama and </span></span><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">interesting than</span></span><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\"> stating &quot;only wicked Centimani don't want to become humans, rest just do they own way\u201d. Boring. </span></span><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">Limiting.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">It's like saying in </span></span><b><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">Mage </span></span></b><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">- &quot;only Scelasti are antagonists to Awakened, rest just strife to common New Atlantis&quot;. It's </span></span><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">unnecessary</span></span><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\"> limiting gameline.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">Not too mentioned that, yes, somehow &quot;typical&quot; players of other splats wanting to spin something in they own kind with other monsters. </span></span><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">Like <b>Mage</b> player coming to \u201c<b>Promethean</b> table\u201d. </span></span><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">I'm not seeing anything evil with crossover game between mage and Promethean characters that aren't looking on questions of humanity \u2013 </span></span><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">for example - </span></span><span style=\"color:#252c2f\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica, Arial, Verdana, sans-serif\">but rather what would they do with they superhuman powers. More things to do with your games.<br /> <br /> And nothing taken from the game as it is, so &quot;purist&quot; <b>Promethean</b> players and ST still can make stories about what it means to be human. Win-win scenaio, for me, don't you think?</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 09-28-2014, 05:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-28T14:38:54-07:00","id":267682,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/263521-phosphorus-the-new-refinement-in-2e?p=267669#post267669\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Mage</b> is great for high transhuman elements, like Singulairty, Strong A.I. or reality bending. But for more &quot;grounded&quot; stuff, like superstrenght, indestructibility or nano treatment the <b>Promethean</b> is far better.</div> </div> </div> </div>Literally every single published major splat can push their &quot;human&quot; traits beyond mortal limits. It's a universal function of high Supernatural Tolerance and a lot of them similarly have a power of one stripe or another that lets them boost their stats on a temporary basis. </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Not to mention what I said before - those of Created that forsake humanity for perfection in they unhuman state make a nice contrast for characters that <b>want </b>to become mortal. It rise questions &quot;why do you really do it&quot;? &quot;Is it more than angels making you&quot;? &quot;Why would any one don't agree with your point&quot;? For me it's much more drama and interesting than stating &quot;only wicked Centimani don't want to become humans, rest just do they own way\u201d. <u>Boring. Limiting.</u> </div> </div> </div>Again, you're making shit up to complain about. Refusers have been an element since the corebook, and in fact one of them is the main antagonist of the Demo game.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm not seeing anything evil with crossover game between mage and Promethean characters that aren't looking on questions of humanity \u2013 for example - but rather what would they do with they superhuman powers. More things to do with your games. </div> </div> </div>The part you're missing: <i>there is absolutely nothing calling for mechanics for &quot;I use the powers the game provides as-written and just kind of do my own thing instead of pursuing understanding of what it means to be human.&quot;</i> That's just called &quot;putting the endgame on indefinite hiatus.&quot; We wouldn't have Verney as a signature character if it wasn't possible.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And nothing taken from the game as it is, so &quot;purist&quot; <b>Promethean</b> players and ST still can make stories about what it means to be human. Win-win scenaio, for me, don't you think? </div> </div> </div><i>You can already do what you're insisting you can't do in 1e.</i></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-28T15:53:05-07:00","id":267732,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/263521-phosphorus-the-new-refinement-in-2e?p=267667#post267667\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thing is, we have rumors sections for that - Strange Alchemies' Refinements chapter has three rumors for each of the five main Refinements, and at least three of those fifteen rumors concern a Promethean becoming something other than human.</div> </div> </div> </div>In particular, one rumor is about Grandfather Crow wanting to become an ordinary crow (Aurum); another is about a Promethean becoming a tree (Cuprum); and a third is about a Promethean becoming a being of pure Pyros (Mercurius). The Ferrum Rumors also include one that could be interpreted as Prometheans Redeeming as Dark Heroes; only Stannum doesn\u2019t mention a variant take on the New Dawn. <br /> <br /> The issue isn\u2019t whether 1e covers the topic somewhere in its supplements; it\u2019s what 2e should cover in its core. I wouldn\u2019t mind a bit of word-count being devoted to the notion of Prometheans who seek New Dawns other than becoming human, though I\u2019d prefer it be presented in the form of \u201cprobably unattainable goals that some Prometheans set for themselves\u201d rather than \u201chere are mechanics for alternative New Dawns\u201d. <br /> <br /> In particular, what I <i>don\u2019t</i> want to see is a New Dawn variant that\u2019s basically \u201ckeep all the good stuff about being a Promethean and toss all the bad stuff\u201d. \u201cBecome an ordinary plant or animal\u201d avoids that particular issue, so I don\u2019t have that much of a problem with the Storyteller actually allowing it to happen (though again, I prefer that sort of ending to be presented as \u201cPrometheans can seek this if they want; but it\u2019s an unattainable goal unless the Storyteller decides otherwise\u201d). <br /> <br /> \u201cBecoming a being of pure Pyros\u201d is something that I wouldn\u2019t mind being a thing in 2e, but not as a conclusion to the Pilgrimage: rather, I like that as a ghost-analog for Prometheans: \u201csometimes, a Promethean who dies while pursuing some great task spawns a <i>qashmal</i> dedicated to completing it; in many cases, the resulting <i>qashmal</i> bears a striking resemblance to the Promethean that spawned it, and some even argue that the <i>qashmal</i> is what passed for the Promethean\u2019s \u2018soul\u2019 \u2014 the Pyros that animated its body \u2014 pushing on toward one last goal before finally dispersing.\u201d<br /> <br /> The Ferrum-style \u201cbecome a superhuman\u201d, though, falls too close to \u201ckeep all the benefits and ditch the drawbacks\u201d for my taste. The closest I\u2019d be willing to go to that is the notion of the \u201cfinal Azoth roll\u201d granting \u2018heric boosts\u2019 to exceptionally successful New Dawns \u2014 with the caveat that the \u2018boosts\u2019 should always be arguably non-supernatural; it shouldn\u2019t be \u201cif you roll well enough at the end, you become transhuman\u201d. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/263521-phosphorus-the-new-refinement-in-2e?p=267667#post267667\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Look at how many people think the inevitable Mage endgame is to archmastery followed by Ascension. Wordcount allocation shapes reader perception.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-28T18:42:53-07:00","id":267802,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u201cBecoming a being of pure Pyros\u201d is something that I wouldn\u2019t mind being a thing in 2e, but not as a conclusion to the Pilgrimage: rather, I like that as a ghost-analog for Prometheans: \u201csometimes, a Promethean who dies while pursuing some great task spawns a <i>qashmal</i> dedicated to completing it; in many cases, the resulting <i>qashmal</i> bears a striking resemblance to the Promethean that spawned it, and some even argue that the <i>qashmal</i> is what passed for the Promethean\u2019s \u2018soul\u2019 \u2014 the Pyros that animated its body \u2014 pushing on toward one last goal before finally dispersing.\u201d </div> </div> </div>I'd like to see this too in a new Promethean Chronicle book... Infact I quite like this idea... Goes quite well with the unifying Principle (see what I did there? ;D) of Azoth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-28T19:01:37-07:00","id":267831,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">What I'm suggesting is, essentially a supplemental book, two, or three, or four or five down the line, as a &quot;Okay, f you as the story teller decide that certain New Dawns other than Human are a thing that can happen, he're how you'd make them work.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn\u2019t mind 2e getting a <b>Mage Chronicler\u2019s Guide</b> book at some point (and yes, I know that <b>Magnum Opus</b> was essentially this for 1e); and mechanics for variants on the New Dawn would fit nicely in such a book. But outside a book explicitly dedicated to \u201cthe following stuff isn\u2019t official, and often contradicts what <i>is</i> official\u201d? No thanks. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Turning into an ordenary plant or animal would be as symple as studying plants/animals instead of humans-probably with alterative versions of refinements.</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019d rather have something like <b>Magnum Opus</b>\u2019 \u201cAnimal Prometheans\u201d for this. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Trans/Superhuman&quot; would probably involve following a refinement that had transmutations that worked a little diferantly from others, require you to max out Azoth, and the end result would be &quot;Basically human, but with a dot or two of Azoth and you can still do transmutations from this specific refinement&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Have you seen my comments in the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/260719-redeemed-as-a-b-splat\">Redeemed as a b-splat</a> thread? I wouldn\u2019t mind a hypothetical <b>Promethean Chronicler\u2019s Guide</b> including an option in it for Redeemed with still-active Athanors who can do some supernatural stuff using Vitriol and Reagent. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rater202</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Promeathean with the bad stuff gone: Here's the idea I've got-It's not actually a Pilgrimage or New Dawn-it's something else, stagnation. it might make it easier, but you'll never earn a <b>real</b> soul. I'm thinking trade offs Okay, you don't generate wasteland anymore, but if you stretch more than 20 miles from such and such place, your pyros goes byby. No more disquiet?Okay, but instead of hating you. mortals forget you as soon as you stop being relevant.</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019m pretty sure we already have a Refinement dedicated to mitigating a Promethean\u2019s inherent drawbacks: Plumbum, I think? (Books not handy; going by memory.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 09-28-2014, 10:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-28T19:04:34-07:00","id":267832,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/263521-phosphorus-the-new-refinement-in-2e?p=267831#post267831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019m pretty sure we already have a Refinement dedicated to mitigating a Promethean\u2019s inherent drawbacks: Plumbum, I think? (Books not handy; going by memory.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Lead is indeed the go-to; favoring Disquietism means that Stannum can pull some of the same load with a smaller time-investment, but the Originists are definitely the ones with the main share of the &quot;mess with your Promethean-ness&quot; market.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-29T02:14:45-07:00","id":268101,"title":"","content":"While intended as antagonists so probably they don't have a full player option write up, I think anyone who wants a redeemed to have some supernatural kick to them could look to alchemists for ideas.<br /> <br /> What could be more natural than a creature of alchemy studying alchemy after becoming human, if they were so inclined? <br /> <br /> Presuming of course that alchemists don't have to chop up prometheans or stick taps in them like maple trees to power their mojo.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-29T04:12:04-07:00","id":268158,"title":"","content":"OK, so:<br /> <br /> 1) Refinements in <b>Promethean 2nd Edition</b> = the 5 from the core + the 4 from <b>Magnum Opus</b> + Phosphorum (want to know what they're about? Go read &quot;The Lesson of the Moth&quot; by Don Marquis. It's short.)<br /> <br /> 2) Centimanus isn't precisely a Refinement. You can't follow the Pilgrimage while you're a Centimanus. <br /> <br /> 3) Sure, you can choose not to follow the Pilgrimage, even while you're on a real Refinement. You pick a Role you like, you stick with it. Maybe you pick the other Roles in that Refinement, even if they're not part of your Pilgrimage, and you master them. There are advantages and disadvantages either way. <br /> <br /> 4) The Great Work makes you human. That's the goal. Lead in gold. The New Dawn. <b>Promethean</b> takes (and always has taken) the explicit view that this is a good thing, and the desire driving the Created, though they may stumble along the way. I, personally, feel the game would suffer if we spent a lot of time saying, &quot;the game is about <i>this</i>, unless you don't want it to be, in which case whatever, have them turn into geese at the end, doesn't matter, robots.&quot; <br /> <br /> Obviously, you <i>can</i> do whatever you want with the game, and I encourage that. But I'm not devoting word count to variants when I barely have enough space to cover what I want to cover. Maybe in a sourcebook, but I'd rather do a <b>Night Horrors</b> book first.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13-blackhatmatt","name":"blackhatmatt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"464"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-29T04:37:26-07:00","id":268165,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackhatmatt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/263521-phosphorus-the-new-refinement-in-2e?p=268158#post268158\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Phosphorum (want to know what they're about? Go read &quot;The Lesson of the Moth&quot; by Don Marquis. It's short.)</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://www.donmarquis.org/themoth.htm\" target=\"_blank\">Link</a> - For those that have lack of Google-Fu. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> So Phosporum is Refinment about Galateid Sainguine Humor? About living the life to the fullest?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-29T06:46:58-07:00","id":268222,"title":"","content":"It was mentioned that there was a newer/better way to just sit and chill (or was the term, 'hide') in your Pilgrimage. I wonder if the Phosphorus refinement is about that. Enjoy your life now as a Promethean, following the brightly burning Azoth, rather than the aching, exhausting Work of your Pilgrimage.<br /> <br /> <br /> EDIT: J/K! Just read the second point &gt;_.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":638,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","user":"reseru","date":". 09-29-2014, 09:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-29T10:36:33-07:00","id":268338,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackhatmatt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/263521-phosphorus-the-new-refinement-in-2e?p=268158#post268158\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1) Refinements in <b>Promethean 2nd Edition</b> = the 5 from the core + the 4 from <b>Magnum Opus</b> + Phosphorum (want to know what they're about? Go read &quot;The Lesson of the Moth&quot; by Don Marquis. It's short.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, that sounds good.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 3) Sure, you can choose not to follow the Pilgrimage, even while you're on a real Refinement. You pick a Role you like, you stick with it. Maybe you pick the other Roles in that Refinement, even if they're not part of your Pilgrimage, and you master them. There are advantages and disadvantages either way. </div> </div> </div>Role, huh? That sounds interesting.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 4) The Great Work makes you human. That's the goal. Lead in gold. The New Dawn. <b>Promethean</b> takes (and always has taken) the explicit view that this is a good thing, and the desire driving the Created, though they may stumble along the way. </div> </div> </div>Also sounds good.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-30T07:23:29-07:00","id":269012,"title":"","content":"Roles sound to me very much like the Nicknames that the Refinements have... As if the roles are in some way acting like the type of person you'd link a Refinement to... Or perhaps something as simple as a practitioner acting in a role that suits the Refinement (like how many factions in books have 'Concepts' listed for them)... Like the Aurum being a very social kind of being... I'm kind of thinking this could link into creating Vitriol beats in a way similar to how the Demon Agendas currently work and get beats by acting in a way that suits the role.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-30T10:31:44-07:00","id":269249,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackhatmatt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/263521-phosphorus-the-new-refinement-in-2e?p=268158#post268158\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">OK, so:<br /> 3) Sure, you can choose not to follow the Pilgrimage, even while you're on a real Refinement. You pick a Role you like, you stick with it. Maybe you pick the other Roles in that Refinement, even if they're not part of your Pilgrimage, and you master them. There are advantages and disadvantages either way.</div> </div> </div> </div> Interresting, so is Roles the way that you hide on the Pilgrimage?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-30T14:02:34-07:00","id":269479,"title":"","content":"Perhaps Roles are a Virtue equivalent then? Something about choosing what you're trying to be?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Cxuog44JenzbN7GaAyRqDO4DXce9VGv6ybaCv9yYsPk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Simulacre: An Alternative Morality Stat for Prometheans</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/9523-the-alchemy-lab-homebrew-athanors\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew Athanors</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/887-metamurpho","name":"Metamurpho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar887_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-01T04:40:06-07:00","id":270043,"title":"","content":"Seeing as from the brief mention of them that there is a list to choose from and you can go through them (at least from what I'm reading and assuming), I wouldn't really think they're Virtues... More likely they'd be a type of persistent condition if they had a mechanical role, I would say so far.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-01T05:42:55-07:00","id":270084,"title":"","content":"Well, &quot;Maybe you pick the other Roles in that Refinement, even if they're not part of your Pilgrimage, and you master them.&quot; implies there's more than one per refinement, but you only follow one at a time, and at least one of them is more important to your character than the rest. Which suggests they're specialisms of a sort - a narrower and more specific approach to the Refinement. But if only a limited number of them (probably one, but it might be more, I suppose) are part of your Pilgrimage, I wonder how that relates to changing Refinement.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-02T13:15:53-07:00","id":271034,"title":"","content":"I'd say it's likely down to what Lineage your character is... It would be good to have more of a link between Lineage and Refinements, I think.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-02T16:20:05-07:00","id":271184,"title":"","content":"Sounds as though Roles are channels within each Refinement, steps on its path. Not exactly ranked, but perhaps fulfilling their potential is one of the universal milestones mentioned elsewhere. Advantages and dis probably does refer to &quot;hiding&quot;, sort of like Cover, the disadvantage meaning that if you do something too out-of-character, you risk deepened Disquiet. People got used to you fitting their stereotype, and then you showed your &quot;true colors&quot;. You were really a &quot;liberal&quot;, or a &quot;tourist&quot;, or &quot;full of airs&quot;. One of those hideous terms used to keep the gates of whatever in-group the Promethean has infiltrated. The advantage is that the Promethean can probably walk undisturbed so long as he toes the line, or carries the flag. These are the recent converts, the gatekeepers, and the aspiring stars of whatever movement. <br /> <br /> For example, Aurum might have a &quot;Congregant&quot; Role. The Congregant joins a church or a temple. She not only follows the strictures, but she enforces them as least as fiercely as any fellow religionist. She garners a reputation as a zealot, but few doubt her faith, and in the time afforded to her, she is appointed an elder. All this time, she provokes next to no Disquiet, or she is able to refocus it on the lapsed and dissident. But one day she slips. She misses a service for some dubious reason, and it's enough to put a crack in her facade. Whispers of her vices begin to circulate, doubts emerge, and the congregation is moved to reclaim itself from her fanaticism, or doubles down on its own orthodoxy in order to liberalize her. Once the in-group has spoken, there's no winning its trust back.<br /> <br /> Still, it's like reading tea leaves. Get to open dev, Matt! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>LFP: Foreign Bodies (Deviant: the Renegades)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/969-verge","name":"Verge","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-02T17:02:29-07:00","id":271206,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Verge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/263521-phosphorus-the-new-refinement-in-2e?p=271184#post271184\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Get to open dev, Matt! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I can second that, go PtC 2e !!! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-04T17:20:51-07:00","id":272588,"title":"","content":"I'm gathering that Roles might be similar to the GotV's Masques in Mage... it's a part to play, a way to fit into the world without being rejected, but it's not really <i>you</i>. The Pilgrimage is about figuring out what it means for you, personally, to be/become human. A Role is just faking it instead of exploring yourself and the world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/747-knowbody","name":"Knowbody","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"391"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-04T22:03:57-07:00","id":272730,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knowbody</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/263521-phosphorus-the-new-refinement-in-2e?p=272588#post272588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm gathering that Roles might be similar to the GotV's Masques in Mage... it's a part to play, a way to fit into the world without being rejected, but it's not really <i>you</i>. The Pilgrimage is about figuring out what it means for you, personally, to be/become human. A Role is just faking it instead of exploring yourself and the world.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or trying a bit &quot;maybe this Role <b>is</b> me&quot;? For me, it looks like &quot;Refinement in action&quot;, human archetypes which Created can assume to look if it <b>their</b> live.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-05T09:11:23-07:00","id":272964,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I rather the notion that the Roles are things the Prometheans try to fit their created existances to, in order to find their 'true' selves. In that way they quest through the Refinements and try and find which suits them best to the Promethean they are and they can see what human role they truly fit into...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3951-wander","name":"wander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"409"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-05T19:09:31-07:00","id":273416,"title":"","content":"I'm kind of glad Centimanus isn't really a refinement anymore...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-06T03:34:27-07:00","id":273565,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackhatmatt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/263521-phosphorus-the-new-refinement-in-2e?p=268158#post268158\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">OK, so:<br /> <br /> 1) Refinements in <b>Promethean 2nd Edition</b> = the 5 from the core + the 4 from <b>Magnum Opus</b> + Phosphorum (want to know what they're about? Go read &quot;The Lesson of the Moth&quot; by Don Marquis. It's short.)</div> </div> </div> </div>So it's the YOLO/Gather-Yee-Rosebuds Refinement?<br /> <br /> <br /> (or how people MISUSE &quot;Carpe Dieum&quot;, which actually means the opposite of what they think it means)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-06T09:08:56-07:00","id":273914,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/263521-phosphorus-the-new-refinement-in-2e?p=273565#post273565\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So it's the YOLO/Gather-Yee-Rosebuds Refinement?<br /> <br /> <br /> (or how people MISUSE &quot;Carpe Dieum&quot;, which actually means the opposite of what they think it means)</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, with a side helping of &quot;gotta die so we can understand life&quot;. <br /> <br /> Fun fact: The pilgrim mark for Phosphorum actually is the letters YOLO spelled all curvy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13-blackhatmatt","name":"blackhatmatt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"464"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-06T15:44:38-07:00","id":274217,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackhatmatt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/263521-phosphorus-the-new-refinement-in-2e?p=273914#post273914\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, with a side helping of &quot;gotta die so we can understand life&quot;.<br /> <br /> Fun fact: The pilgrim mark for Phosphorum actually is the letters YOLO spelled all curvy.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I can't remember his name - but the Osirian who kept dying to explore the &quot;river of death&quot; - last edition he pretty much defaulted into Argentum, would that exploration now be Phosphorum?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member"